[Music]  it's the last weekend to drive through  the Tropicana exit before ndot's major  Tropicana project causes some major  changes this week Victoria Saha spoke  with ndot and explains  Tropicana will be turning into Tropicana  Southern Nevada Department of  Transportation takes down half of the  Tropicana flyover heading into the strip  right now it's too low it doesn't beat  Federal height requirements Justin  Hopkins with ndot says this project  won't finish until 2025. he says the  Tropicana overpass on I-15 often gets  hit by large trucks and once that's  fixed there are more lanes that will be  added so it's going to go from three  lanes in both directions to four lanes  in both directions all the way from Las  Vegas Boulevard to Valley View we're  also making a number of pedestrian  improvements including taking the  sidewalks from five feet to 10 new  lighting making it more pedestrian  friendly when it comes to events  Allegiant and T-Mobile Arena the  Tropicana project will include closing  the I-15 both ways on Tropicana are for  eight days starting January 22nd through  the 30th it will also include a  three-day closure of I-15 in both  directions between Flamingo and Russell  starting January 27th ndot says they  have come out with an app that you can  download to keep up to date with  construction and to find another way to  get around the cutoff for the last car  to travel through the Tropicana exit  will be Tuesday at 11 PM Victoria Saha 8  news now now as Victoria mentioned this  whole project will last until 2025 and  will cost over 300 million dollars  Victoria also asked how this would  affect the Super Bowl coming to town  next year ndot says they have plans in  place to help traffic but those will be  released closer to the big game

